"Virtual Memory is a memory management technique that creates an illusion of a large main memory by using the disk as additional memory. Paging works by dividing the main memory into fixed-size blocks called pages, which can be swapped out to disk when they are not in use. Page faults occur when a program attempts to access a page that is currently stored on disk and cannot be found in RAM.

