"Virtual Memory is a technique used by operating systems (OS) to manage limited physical memory resources. It creates an illusion of having more main memory than actually exists on the system. This allows programs to access larger amounts of data without needing additional hardware storage.

Paging works as follows:
- When a program tries to read or write a block of memory that is not currently in RAM, it triggers a page fault.
